ey likely missed the board entirely or have a weak pair.\nA King kicker is quite strong in a "battle of high cards".\n\nHowever, betting here has little value. A worse hand (like Q-high or lower) will likely fold to a bet. A better hand (any pair, any 5, or A-high) might call or raise. If I check, I likely win against random trash hands, or lose a small pot if they have an Ace or a Pair.\n\nSince the opponent checked the River to me, I can just check back and Showdown. There is no need to bluff (I have showdown value) and no clear value bet (worse hands fold, better hands call).\n\nReason: The board contains three fives. My hand is Three of a Kind with a King kicker. The opponent has shown passivity throughout the hand, checking every street. Betting is unlikely to get called by worse hands, and checking guarantees seeing a showdown without risking more chips against a trapped Full House or Quads (though unlikely). Checking is the safest and most efficient play to realize my equity.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
